# Arguments passed to the tier-node daemon (word-split by systemd).
#
# The mesh is bootstrapped from a single reachable seed; membership is then
# learned via gossip, so one working seed is enough for a node to join.
#
# Listen only, no bootstrap:
TIER_ARGS=run 7777
#
# Bootstrap against a seed (IPv4 or IPv6 literal, port as a separate token):
#   TIER_ARGS=run 7777 203.0.113.10 7777
#   TIER_ARGS=run 7777 2001:db8::10 7777
#
# The daemon binds the IPv6 wildcard (dual-stack), so it listens on both IPv6
# and IPv4 at the given port.
